// Rest: tiredness, and resting it off (AGENCY.md §6).
//
// Cut points:
// - full:     felt tiredness above 50 raises getting some rest: eight hours
//             lying down, which clears fatigue.
// - reduced:  the same, decided on the cadence's beat; a rest runs at full
//             pace.
// - abstract: as reduced.
// - frozen:   it doesn't decide; a rest under way waits.
// - body:     fatigue is things.tri's (#Agent): effort raises it (an
//             operation's `exertion`), and so do freezing and smothering
//             (src/domains_bodies.odin); it is felt by bands of 10. Starving
//             doesn't tire (hunger/body.tri), so resting doesn't mend it.
// - air:      a rest watches the air over it: it wakes when the carbon
//             dioxide reaches the command's amount, or the temperature
//             leaves what the breather rests easy in (air/air.tri).
// - code:     the watch on the air is any activity's that is a #Resting
//             (src/act_actions.odin), and what breathes breathes as at
//             rest through one (src/domains_atmosphere.odin). That
//             fatigue is gone is declared.

package rest

// Tiredness raises resting: worth what the agent feels of it; done once a
// rest has run its course.
rest_when_tired: #Goal & {
    title:   "get some rest"
    done:    #Did & { did: "while_away" }
    pressed: { need: "tired", above: 50 }
    worth:   [#Need & { pressure: "tired", per: 5 }]
} @family(goals)

lie_down: #Method & {
    title: "lie down"
    goal:  "rest_when_tired"
    rank:  1
    pre:   { find: [], match: #Frame & { me: #Agent & { id: $me, place: #OnTile } } }
    steps: [#Do & { op: "while_away" }]
} @family(methods)

// Resting: rested through, fatigue is gone, however long the rest was.
// Through it, what breathes breathes as at rest, and there is a watch on
// the air: woken when its carbon dioxide reaches the command's amount
// (mmol; 4,000 if none). Whatever is passed at ease is one: a night's
// sleep (home/), minding a stall (market/), lying in wait (hunting/), an
// animal grazing or bedded down.
#Resting: #Operation & {
    after: { actor: #Agent & { fatigue: 0 } }
}

// Rest a while, 8 hours.
while_away: #Resting & {
    duration: 8h
    uses:     ["hands", "legs"]
    roles:    { actor: #Agent & { place: #OnTile } }
} @family(operations)
